    { "file": "tools/style/refresh/scope.sh", "line": 2, "current": "# Build the four refresh work-lists (A/B/C/D) for an EUDPA code-style review", "classification": "GENERICISE", "proposed": "# Build the four refresh work-lists (A/B/C/D) for a code-style review", "why": "Header prose baking the Jira project key into the description of a generic tool. The script itself is project-agnostic apart from the arg matcher. Comment-only, zero behaviour risk. R6 keeps EUDPA functional; this is not a functional use." },

    { "file": "tools/ticket/setup-branch.sh", "line": 43, "current": "        EUDPA-*)", "classification": "REVIEW", "proposed": "Introduce a single source of truth for the ticket-key prefix — e.g. TICKET_PREFIX=\"${TICKET_PREFIX:-EUDPA}\" sourced from one shared workspace config file that all 20 hardcode sites read, defaulting to EUDPA so today's behaviour is unchanged.", "why": "R6 says EUDPA stays functional but asks where it is hardcoded. This is the most load-bearing of the 20 sites: it both gates the positional arg AND feeds the generated branch name feat/EUDPA-X-<slug>. A second commodity line on a different Jira project would silently fail arg parsing here with 'Unknown arg'. Human must rule on where the shared config lives (env var vs a tools/lib/ sourced file vs tim) before anyone touches 20 files." },
